# Semantic layer

`lib/semantic` is a pure TypeScript kernel: no React, no `app/api`, no cycles.

- Input errors throw; do not swallow them (`catch { continue; }` in ORDER BY already hides a real bug — do not copy that).
- One formula grammar: `tokenizeCalcExpr` / `parseCalcExpr` in planner, reused by `expressionEngine.ts`.
- A new operator or dialect needs a unit test for each affected dialect: `postgres`, `clickhouse`, `mssql`. `SqlDialect` has no `mysql` today — do not pretend it does.
- Changing `.snap` requires a line-by-line SQL explanation in the PR. `planner.golden` currently pins a missing ORDER BY for an explicit measure sort.
- Two model factories exist (`SchemaIntelligenceService` and `buildAutoSemanticModel`). Changing type inference in one without the other is a defect unless the PR says why.
- After planner changes run `cd dashboard && npm test -- src/lib/semantic`.
